p, also known as banana sauce (in export markets), is a Philippine fruit ketchup condiment made from banana, sugar, vinegar, and spices. Its natural color is brownish-yellow but it is often dyed red to resemble tomato ketchup. Banana ketchup was first produced in the Philippines during World War II due to a shortage of tomatoes but a comparatively high production of bananas."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-banana-ketchup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_ketchup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine"],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao"],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Banana","ingredient/banana"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Panlasang Pinoy","ref":"site/panlasangpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"panlasangpinoy.com","note":"Vanjo Merano's large library of Filipino recipes and cooking videos.","url":"https://panlasangpinoy.com/filipino-food/","suggested":true},{"name":"Kawaling Pinoy","ref":"site/kawalingpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kawalingpinoy.com","note":"Lalaine Manalo's blog of Filipino home cooking.","url":"https://www.kawalingpinoy.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Flavours of Iloilo","ref":"site/flavoursofiloilo-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com","note":"Blog of Ilonggo home dishes from Iloilo in the Western Visayas.","url":"https://flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com/2013/05/how-about-some-chicken-binakol.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Filipino cuisine","links":[["Adobo (Filipino dish)","dish/adobo-filipino-dish"],["Aparon","dish/aparon"],["Champorado","dish/champorado"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Filipino barbecue","dish/filipino-barbecue"],["Food for the gods","dish/food-for-the-gods"],["Isaw","dish/isaw"],["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"],["Kadyos, manok, kag ubad","dish/kadyos-manok-kag-ubad"],["Kumukunsi","dish/kumukunsi"],["Mango float","dish/mango-float"],["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"],["Pastil","dish/pastil"],["Piaparan","dish/piaparan"],["Pilipit","dish/pilipit"],["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"],["Sushi bake","dish/sushi-bake"],["Tortang talong","dish/tortang-talong"]]}]},"dish/caravaggio-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/caravaggio-restaurant","n":"Caravaggio (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Caravaggio is an Italian restaurant located at 23 East 74th Street (between 5th Avenue and Madison Avenue) on the Upper East Side in Manhattan, in New York City.  It is around the corner from the Met Breuer."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-caravaggio-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caravaggio_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba","dish/antica-pizzeria-port-alba"],["Antico Pizza","dish/antico-pizza"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["ASK Italian","dish/ask-italian"],["Asti (restaurant)","dish/asti-restaurant"],["Ava Gene's","dish/ava-gene-s"],["Bamonte's","dish/bamonte-s"],["Bar del Corso","dish/bar-del-corso"],["Barbetta","dish/barbetta"],["Barbuto (restaurant)","dish/barbuto-restaurant"],["Bella Italia","dish/bella-italia"],["Beppi's Restaurant","dish/beppi-s-restaurant"],["Bertucci's","dish/bertucci-s"],["BiCE Ristorante","dish/bice-ristorante"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Black' Smith","dish/black-smith"],["Bocca di Lupo","dish/bocca-di-lupo"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Buca di Beppo","dish/buca-di-beppo"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caffé Vittoria","dish/caffe-vittoria"],["Camille's (Providence, Rhode Island)","dish/camille-s-providence-rhode-island"],["Campisi's Egyptian Restaurant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"]]}]},"dish/chaku-newari-cuisine":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/chaku-newari-cuisine","n":"Chaku (Newari cuisine)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Newari cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Chaku is a confectionery made by Newar people and is popular in the Kathmandu Valley. It is made from concentrated sugarcane juice, jaggery, ghee, and nuts. The mixture is cooked until it attains a solid form, and then pulled on a hook in a manner similar to making taffy and then cut into small rolls. It may also be cooked in a shallow dish and cut into small diamond-shaped pieces. Chaku may be eaten separately, or it can also be used in making Yomari (योमरी)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chaku-newari-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaku_(Newari_cuisine)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Newari cuisine","cuisine/newari-cuisine"]]}]},"dish/chitranna":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/chitranna","n":"Chitranna","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Karnataka cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Chitranna, also known as Lemon rice, is a rice-based dish widely prepared in South India. It is prepared by mixing cooked rice with a special seasoning called Oggarane or Gojju. Characteristic of the seasoning are mustard seeds, fried lentils, peanuts, curry leaves, chillies, lemon juice and other optional items such as  scrapes of unripe mango. Added turmeric powder gives Chitranna its yellow color. Garlic and onions are also used in the seasoning by some, although traditionally they do not form part of the recipe."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chitranna"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chitranna"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Karnataka cuisine","cuisine/karnataka-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Dassana's Veg Recipes (Punjabi)","ref":"site/vegrecipesofindia-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vegrecipesofindia.com","note":"Karnataka section of Dassana Amit's Indian vegetarian recipe blog.","url":"https://www.vegrecipesofindia.com/recipes/karnataka-cuisine/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chitra's Food Book","ref":"site/chitrasfoodbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"chitrasfoodbook.com","note":"Karnataka recipes on a South Indian home cook's vegetarian blog.","url":"https://www.chitrasfoodbook.com/recipes/karnataka-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Karnataka cuisine","links":[["Majjige huli","dish/majjige-huli"],["Pundi","dish/pundi"],["Vangibath","dish/vangibath"]]}]},"dish/croquembouche":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/croquembouche","n":"Croquembouche","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A croquembouche or croque-en-bouche is a French dessert consisting of choux pastry puffs piled into a cone and bound with threads of caramel. In Italy and France, it is often served at weddings, baptisms and First Communions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-croquembouche"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croquembouche"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Caramel","ingredient/caramel"],["Profiterole","ingredient/profiterole"],["Profiteroles","ingredient/profiteroles"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an eart