, pickling, and seedless."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cucumbers"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumbers"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"],["Kvass","ingredient/kvass"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Sausage","ingredient/sausage"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Smetana","ingredient/smetana"],["Sour cream","ingredient/sour-cream"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]]}]},"dish/pasta-mollicata":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pasta-mollicata","n":"Pasta mollicata","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Sicilian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pasta mollicata is a pasta dish based on breadcrumbs, particularly common in the Basilicata, Calabria, and Sicily regions of Italy. Compared to other pasta recipes, it is considered a \"poor dish\" because it is not prepared with many ingredients."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pasta-mollicata"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasta_mollicata"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Breadcrumbs","ingredient/breadcrumbs"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"]]},{"h":"More from Sicilian cuisine","links":[["Busiate","dish/busiate"],["Cassatella di Agira","dish/cassatella-di-agira"],["Crocchè","dish/crocche"],["Iris (pastry)","dish/iris-pastry"],["Maccu","dish/maccu"],["Panella","dish/panella"],["Pani câ meusa","dish/pani-ca-meusa"],["Parmigiana","dish/parmigiana"],["Pasta alla Norma","dish/pasta-alla-norma"],["Pasta con le sarde","dish/pasta-con-le-sarde"],["Stigghiola","dish/stigghiola"]]}]},"dish/patatnik":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/patatnik","n":"Patatnik","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Bulgarian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Patatnik or patetnik is a Bulgarian potato dish characteristic of the Rhodope Mountains in the country's central south. Patatnik is made of grated potatoes, onions, salt and a type of very mild mint called gyosum in Bulgarian, all mixed and cooked on a slow fire. Some restaurants add sirene (white cheese) or eggs, but this is not traditional; some people also use savory and peppers."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-patatnik"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patatnik"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Spearmint","ingredient/spearmint"]]},{"h":"More from Bulgarian cuisine","links":[["Banitsa","dish/banitsa"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Garash cake","dish/garash-cake"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Lyutenitsa","dish/lyutenitsa"],["Pindjur","dish/pindjur"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tarator","dish/tarator"]]}]},"dish/pao-na-chapa":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pao-na-chapa","n":"Pão na chapa","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Brazilian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Pão na chapa is a Brazilian breakfast food that is popular in the state of São Paulo. The dish consists of a piece of pão francês cut in half and spread in butter, then pressed in the griddle or cooked in a pan. It is also common to spread requeijão on the bread and drink coffee (normally café au lait) alongside it."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pao-na-chapa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P%C3%A3o_na_chapa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[